.TH TMPMAIL 1 "August 2026" "tmpmail 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tmpmail \- fast multi-backend temporary email
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tmpmail
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
tmpmail creates and monitors named disposable inboxes through Mail.tm and
DropMail. With no command it lists messages for the active inbox.
.SH COMMON COMMANDS
.TP
.B tmpmail new [NAME]
Create an inbox. This is an alias for inbox create.
.TP
.B tmpmail [message list]
List messages in the active or selected inbox.
.TP
.B tmpmail read MESSAGE [--peek] [--html [--open]]
Render one message. Successful output acknowledges it unless --peek is used.
.TP
.B tmpmail latest
Render exactly the newest message in one inbox.
.TP
.B tmpmail message new [--all-inboxes] [--review]
List every locally unseen message without acknowledging it.
.TP
.B tmpmail attachment save MESSAGE ATTACHMENT [--force]
Safely stream an attachment into the current directory.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --inbox NAME
Select a saved inbox for this command.
.TP
.B --provider PROVIDER, --no-provider PROVIDER
Pin or exclude a provider for inbox creation.
.TP
.B --json
Emit the stable tmpmail/v1 JSON envelope and never prompt.
.TP
.B --timeout DURATION
Set the total network deadline using an ms or s suffix.
.SH SECURITY
Mail bodies, headers, and filenames are treated as untrusted. HTML is rendered
as text unless an inert cached representation is explicitly requested. Secret
tokens are accepted through secure input or stdin, never ordinary arguments.
.SH PROVIDERS
Mail.tm functionality is powered by Mail.tm (https://mail.tm). DropMail requires
a current user-supplied API token.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR open (1),
.BR xdg-open (1)
